{
  "version": 1,
  "generator": "tests/story_bench.c (make story)",
  "policy": "A relay keeper who reads the gauges, not the code, and does not hear Kit's call (her reading reaches it only as a steadier speed readout). Far from the mark it reads the wobbling speed readout as the speed the turn will coast to once the motor spins down, and aims for the lower of its cruising speed (0.34-0.60 c) and the speed it could still brake from over the distance left, less a margin of 5-35 %; it runs the motor towards the mark below that aim, against the turn above it, and coasts within 0.02-0.06 c of it. A new command takes after 2-5 frames (0.4-1.0 t). Within 2.0 units of the mark it reads the position marker instead (it does not wobble) and creeps in at 0.04-0.10 c; within 0.8 it lets the turn stop and waits for the catch arm. On a held bell it cuts the motor and waits. Its hand is re-drawn from the night's own stirred seed for every leg and after every failure. Choices follow the path field.",
  "crisis": "the cell gauge in the red (charge below 0.30) at any moment in the leg, or a failure (a failure counts as a crisis)",
  "failure": "the cell ran dry (Kit cranks it, or after the cut the turn is lost), the turn ran off the posts or wandered 200 t without a held mark and was relaunched, or it struck a catch arm too fast and jammed the motor",
  "segments": ["to the weir", "to the bell", "back to the gorge", "the water in the hut", "up to the dam road"],
  "note": "16 seeds x 12 nights; every night has its own stirred seed; the path comes from the night number.",
